From: LukeValen <panvk-eden@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 112] panfrost: enable R5G5B5A1 sampling on Valhall

Expose the exact A1/BGR5 packed texture encoding already present in the
Valhall genxml as sample/transfer-only support for PIPE_FORMAT_A1B5G5R5.
This makes VK_FORMAT_R5G5B5A1_UNORM_PACK16 usable by Eden without claiming
render-target or storage support.

Target: Eden Android / Mali-G615 MC6 / PAN_ARCH 11

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_format.c b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_format.c
index 039f096..71337b4 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_format.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_format.c
@@ -331,6 +331,12 @@ const struct pan_format GENX(pan_pipe_format)[PIPE_FORMAT_COUNT] = {
    FMT(R5G5B5X1_UNORM,          RGB5_A1_UNORM,   RGB1, L, VT__IB),
    FMT(B5G5R5X1_UNORM,          RGB5_A1_UNORM,   BGR1, L, VT__IB),
    FMT(R5G5B5A1_UNORM,          RGB5_A1_UNORM,   RGBA, L, VTR_IB),
+   /* VK_FORMAT_R5G5B5A1_UNORM_PACK16 maps to PIPE_FORMAT_A1B5G5R5_UNORM.
+    * Valhall exposes the exact A1/BGR5 packed texture encoding; advertise it
+    * for sampling/transfer only.  Eden uses this format for Switch
+    * A5B5G5R1 textures (notably observed in Breath of the Wild).
+    */
+   FMT(A1B5G5R5_UNORM,          A1_BGR5_UNORM,   RGBA, L, _T____),
    FMT(B5G5R5A1_UNORM,          RGB5_A1_UNORM,   BGRA, L, VTR_IB),
    FMT(R10G10B10X2_UNORM,       RGB10_A2_UNORM,  RGB1, L, VTR_IB),
    FMT(B10G10R10X2_UNORM,       RGB10_A2_UNORM,  BGR1, L, VTR_IB),
